  "result": "Perfect! The dates module has been successfully implemented with all tests passing. Here's a summary:\n\n## Date Utilities Implementation\n\n**Created src/dates.js with three UTC-aware date functions:**\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`** - Validates dates in YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Checks format with regex\n   - Validates actual date values (e.g., rejects Feb 30)\n   - All checks done in UTC\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`** - Adds/subtracts days from a date\n   - Returns result in YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Handles month boundaries correctly\n   - Handles leap years\n   - Uses UTC for all calculations\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`** - Calculates days between two dates\n   - Returns whole days (b minus a)\n   - Handles negative differences\n   - Uses UTC for all calculations\n\n**Changes made:**\n- Removed the local `isValidDate` helper from invoices.js\n- Updated invoices.js to import `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- createInvoice now uses the shared isValidDate function\n\n**Test Coverage (20 new tests):**\n- \u2714 isValidDate: 6 tests covering valid dates, invalid formats, invalid dates, non-string input, empty strings, spaces\n- \u2714 addDays: 6 tests covering positive/negative days, month boundaries, leap years, zero days, format validation\n- \u2714 daysBetween: 7 tests covering positive/negative differences, same date, whole days, year boundaries, leap years\n- \u2714 Integration: 1 test verifying addDays and daysBetween are inverses\n\n**Test Results:**\n- Total tests: 153\n- Passing: 148 \u2714\n- Failing: 5 (pre-existing VAT-related tests)\n\nAll date utility tests pass successfully. The dates module now provides a centralized place for all date operations in the application, with consistent UTC handling throughout.",
